# Broad env exclusion so `.env.production`, `.env.staging`, etc.
# don't slip through the prior `.env` / `.env.local` / `.env.*.local`
# trio. The `!.env.example` negation keeps the committed template
# (used by `.env.example → .env` bootstrap) reachable.
*.env*
!.env.example
